# Branch Zero — environment variable NAMES only. Never commit real keys.
#
# Three local files (all git-ignored except this example):
#   .env              — laptop: Vite + both desks + infra scripts (full catalog below)
#   .env.teller-live  — Docker Live desk only (TELLER_ENV_FILE=…); no VITE_ / lab / iNPC
#   .env.web-live     — Cloudflare Pages build mirror; PUBLIC VITE_* only (no desk secrets)
#
# Remote EVM (chain 1337) uses Ganache-parity keys that MUST NEVER touch a public network.

# ---- chains ----
# The Teller Desk pins one chain at boot (docs/SEPOLIA-LIVE.md §2). Two desks run side by side:
#
#   Live (product default)  CHAIN_ID=11155111  PORT=8787      npm run dev:teller       -> Vite /api
#   Dev  (Developer Mode)   --dev  (or 1337)   DEV_PORT=8788   npm run dev:teller:dev   -> Vite /dev-api
#   Arc  (U6, DEFERRED)     CHAIN_ID=5042002   ARC_PORT=8789                            -> Vite /arc-api
#
# CHAIN_ID unset means LIVE. The Dev desk is chosen with the `--dev` flag rather than an env var so both
# desks can be started from package.json on any shell (cmd.exe has no `VAR=x cmd` prefix), and so the two
# processes cannot inherit each other's port. Live/Dev is NOT the Arc elevator and NOT MockChain (`?mock=`).
CHAIN_ID=11155111
SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=
REMOTE_EVM_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545
# Tailscale Serve alternative (hostname stays local, never committed):
# REMOTE_EVM_RPC_URL=https://<host>.<tailnet>.ts.net
ARC_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
# Largest gas limit any single transaction may declare. 2^24 is the Remote EVM block limit AND the `rpc.gascap`
# public Sepolia providers use, and it is just enough for CopyBlox.cloneBlox (~16.65M measured). A provider that
# caps lower makes Account Opening fail loudly; raise this only against an RPC that really allows more.
MAX_TX_GAS=16777216

# ---- keys (infra/ + Teller Desk) ----
# Remote EVM dev mapping (docs/REMOTE-EVM.md §2): deployer=acct0, broadcaster=acct1, recovery=acct2, manager=acct3, player owner=acct4.
# Private keys live in particle-tool-box/Docker Apps/Remote EVM/ganache-deterministic-accounts.json — paste locally, never here.
DEPLOYER_PK=
BROADCASTER_PK=
MANAGER_PK=
# Sepolia (11155111) — the LIVE wing. Throwaway keys, separate from every Remote EVM / Arc / ENS key.
# Fund SEPOLIA_TREASURY_PK from Google Cloud ETH + Circle USDC first; staff wallets get need × 1.25 top-ups
# (docs/SEPOLIA-TREASURY.md). `npm -w infra run funding:sepolia` lists balances vs need.
# NEVER paste Ganache-parity keys here — infra and the desk both refuse them, by derived address.
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_PK=
# Read-only alternative: watch a treasury this process holds no key for (balances + plan, never a send).
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_ADDRESS=
# Background rebalancing: `on` (default when the key is present) tops staff wallets before an Account Opening
# and on an interval; `off` leaves `npm run treasury:topup` as the only way money moves. Never read on Dev.
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_AUTO=on
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_INTERVAL_SEC=900
# Baseline need per role, in ETH. target = need x 1.25 (the margin is fixed by the principal). Defaults are
# measured, not optimistic: cloneBlox is ~16.65M gas ~ 0.0425 ETH at S2 fees, so the deployer dwarfs the rest.
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_NEED_DEPLOYER_ETH=0.048
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_NEED_BROADCASTER_ETH=0.012
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_NEED_MANAGER_ETH=0.008
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_NEED_REGISTRAR_ETH=0.008
# Drain guards: no single transfer above per-tx, no more than per-hour in a rolling hour (a shared ledger in
# apps/teller-desk/.data), and always keep the reserve so the treasury can pay for its own transfers.
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_MAX_TX_ETH=0.05
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_MAX_HOUR_ETH=0.12
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_RESERVE_ETH=0.001
# Practice-dollar float. `off`: the Live practice token is open-mint, so the deployer makes its own float.
# Circle's USDC is collected and displayed but NEVER sent by any policy - it is a different token.
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_PRACTICE=off
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_NEED_PRACTICE_USDC=500
# Demo-only: accept the treasury sharing a key with a staff role. Every treasury path REFUSES that collapse
# by derived address unless this is `on`, and prints/reports it when it is (docs/SEPOLIA-TREASURY.md 1).
SEPOLIA_TREASURY_ALLOW_ROLE_REUSE=off
SEPOLIA_DEPLOYER_PK=
SEPOLIA_BROADCASTER_PK=
SEPOLIA_MANAGER_PK=
SEPOLIA_RECOVERY_ADDRESS=
# Public addresses derived from the Live keys (funding reports / dashboards; never secrets).
SEPOLIA_OWNER_ADDRESS=
SEPOLIA_BROADCASTER_ADDRESS=
SEPOLIA_MANAGER_ADDRESS=
# Arc Testnet (5042002) — DEFERRED. Keys stay separate from every Remote EVM / ENS key. Never Ganache-parity.
ARC_DEPLOYER_PK=
ARC_BROADCASTER_PK=
ARC_MANAGER_PK=
# Lab / Remote EVM addresses (public) used by scripts when no key is needed:
OWNER_ADDRESS=0xd03ea8624C8C5987235048901fB614fDcA89b117
BROADCASTER_ADDRESS=0xFFcf8FDEE72ac11b5c542428B35EEF5769C409f0
RECOVERY_ADDRESS=0x22d491Bde2303f2f43325b2108D26f1eAbA1e32b
ARC_OWNER_ADDRESS=
ARC_BROADCASTER_ADDRESS=
ARC_RECOVERY_ADDRESS=

# ---- account params ----
TIMELOCK_SEC=120
# Opening balance handed to a freshly provisioned account, in display units of the demo token.
OPENING_BALANCE_USDC=500
# Lane A soft cap (off-chain routing only; see docs/REFLECTION.md 2.2). Above this it is a wire (Lane B, U2).
INSTANT_LIMIT_USDC=100
# U2 Lane B option 1: the player's embedded wallet sends executeWithTimeLock / approve / cancel itself, so it
# needs gas. The deployer tops it up to this amount at Account Opening (native units; Arc native USDC is 18 decimals).
# Per-wing override wins: on Sepolia 0.05 ETH is a whole day's faucet drop per player, while a wire plus a release
# is ~450k gas (<0.0015 ETH), so LIVE defaults to 0.003. The lab chain keeps 0.05 because dev ETH is free.
OWNER_GAS_ETH=0.05
SEPOLIA_OWNER_GAS_ETH=0.003
# U4+ Priority release (G5b). on = Mr. Walker may submit an owner-signed meta-approve BEFORE releaseTime once the
# player passes a Passkey (hand scan); needs MANAGER_PK. off = vault-only accounts (U2 invariant: no META_APPROVE
# bits on transfer, the clock is the only way out). Default: on when MANAGER_PK is set. Re-check re-syncs grants.
PRIORITY_RELEASE=on
EVENT_FORWARDER=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# ---- one-time chain bootstrap (npm run chain:bootstrap) ----
# Path to a BUILT Bloxchain-Protocol checkout. Read only for already-compiled artifact JSON (CopyBlox,
# BasicERC20), which is deployed unchanged and recorded in infra/deployments/. Nothing in apps/ uses it.
BLOXCHAIN_PROTOCOL_DIR=

# ---- historical U0 compiler (not the ongoing product path; leave unset) ----
# SOLC_EVM_VERSION=prague

# ---- teller desk (one port per wing; the Vite proxies in apps/web/vite.config.ts match these) ----
# HOST=127.0.0.1  # bind address. Leave unset on a laptop (loopback only, behind the Vite proxy). The Docker image
#                 # sets HOST=0.0.0.0 itself so the container port mapping works (docs/HOSTING.md).
PORT=8787          # Live  (Sepolia)      -> /api
DEV_PORT=8788      # Dev   (Remote EVM)   -> /dev-api      npm run dev:teller:dev
ARC_PORT=8789      # Arc   (DEFERRED)     -> /arc-api
# CORS allowlist (exact origins). Laptop Vite: localhost:5173. Hackathon Caddy: 127.0.0.1:8080 / localhost:8080.
# Public: https://branchzero.app (+ www if used). Never `*`.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:8080,http://localhost:8080,https://branchzero.app
# Laptop / compose same-origin. Pages production uses an absolute desk URL in `.env.web-live` instead.
VITE_TELLER_DESK_URL=/api
# VITE_GAME_BASE_URL=https://game.branchzero.app/<version>   # R2 twin only; unset = same-origin /game
#                                                          # lean export (Profile H) fits Pages without R2
#                                                          # (`npm run export:web:lean`, docs/HOSTING.md §3.3)
#                                                          # hackathon compose forces /api + /game via build:web:hackathon
VITE_DEV_TELLER_DESK_URL=/dev-api
VITE_ARC_TELLER_DESK_URL=/arc-api

# ---- Live desk-only env file (recommended for Docker) ----
# Prefer a desk-scoped file so the container does not inherit browser / iNPC / lab / Remote EVM keys:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.teller-live   # then copy Live values from your .env (see list below)
#   TELLER_ENV_FILE=.env.teller-live docker compose up -d teller-live
#   TELLER_ENV_FILE=.env.teller-live docker compose -f docker-compose.hackathon.yml up -d --build
#
# `.env.teller-live` is git-ignored. Never commit it.
# Put in `.env.teller-live` (Live wing only):
#   SEPOLIA_RPC_URL, SEPOLIA_DEPLOYER_PK, SEPOLIA_BROADCASTER_PK, SEPOLIA_MANAGER_PK, SEPOLIA_RECOVERY_ADDRESS
#   SEPOLIA_TREASURY_PK (+ optional SEPOLIA_TREASURY_* knobs), SEPOLIA_OWNER_GAS_ETH
#   ENS_PARENT_NAME, ENS_REGISTRAR_PK
#   PRIVY_APP_ID, PRIVY_APP_SECRET, PRIVY_AUTHORIZATION_KEY, PRIVY_SIGNER_ID, optional PRIVY_POLICY_ID
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS, PORT, CHAIN_ID=11155111
#   TIMELOCK_SEC, OPENING_BALANCE_USDC, INSTANT_LIMIT_USDC, PRIORITY_RELEASE, MAX_TX_GAS (optional)
#   optional GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID / GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
# Leave OUT of `.env.teller-live`: unprefixed DEPLOYER_PK/BROADCASTER_PK (lab), REMOTE_EVM_*, ARC_*,
# VITE_*, OPENROUTER_*, INPC_*, TUNNEL_TOKEN (tunnel token stays in repo-root `.env` for Compose interpolation).

# ---- Cloudflare Pages / hosted shell build env (public VITE_* only) ----
# Paste into Pages → Settings → Environment variables (Production + Preview), or keep `.env.web-live`:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.web-live   # then fill VITE_* / public ids only from your .env
#
# NEVER put desk secrets here: no PRIVY_APP_SECRET, PRIVY_AUTHORIZATION_KEY, SEPOLIA_*_PK, ENS_REGISTRAR_PK, TUNNEL_TOKEN.
#
# Required on Pages (docs/HOSTING.md §3.1):
#   NODE_VERSION=22
#   VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID=
#   VITE_PRIVY_SIGNER_ID=
#   VITE_TELLER_DESK_URL=https://desk.branchzero.app
# Optional:
#   VITE_GAME_BASE_URL=…          # only if wasm stays on R2; leave unset after export:web:lean
#   VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
#   VITE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=         # public RPC baked into the shell if the build uses it

# ---- hackathon all-in-one stack (docs/HOSTING.md 4; docker-compose.hackathon.yml) ----
# Compose interpolates these from the *project* `.env` (not from TELLER_ENV_FILE). TUNNEL_TOKEN is a SECRET:
# git-ignored, never a build arg, never an image layer. Desk secrets still come from TELLER_ENV_FILE.
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# CADDY_BIND=127.0.0.1
# CADDY_PORT=8080
# CADDY_IMAGE=caddy:2.11-alpine
# CLOUDFLARED_IMAGE=cloudflare/cloudflared:2026.9.1
# TELLER_ENV_FILE=.env.teller-live

# ---- privy (U1) ----
PRIVY_APP_ID=
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=
PRIVY_AUTHORIZATION_KEY=
PRIVY_POLICY_ID=
PRIVY_SIGNER_ID=

# ---- web (Vite, prefixed) ----
# VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID must match PRIVY_APP_ID; VITE_PRIVY_SIGNER_ID must match PRIVY_SIGNER_ID.
# Never put PRIVY_APP_SECRET or PRIVY_AUTHORIZATION_KEY in VITE_* vars.
VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID=
VITE_PRIVY_SIGNER_ID=
# Optional public Sepolia RPC for shell reads (baked into the client if set).
VITE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=
# Leave VITE_TELLER_DESK_URL empty or `/api` in laptop dev (Vite proxy). Pages: see `.env.web-live`.

# ---- GitHub star CTAs (front door ★) — optional ----
# Create an OAuth App: https://github.com/settings/developers
# Callback URL must be exactly: http://localhost:5173/github-oauth.html  (plus your deployed origin)
# Client ID is public (Vite); client secret stays on the Teller Desk only.
# Without these, the buttons open the repo in a new tab for a manual Star.
# VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=          # same value as VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID
# GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ---- ENS (U5 / ENG-0007) — Sepolia only in BOTH modes; never Ganache or mainnet keys ----
# Parent branchzero.eth is registered on ENSv2 (K6 yes). Pin UR V2 0x85ed…b92cf in desk resolve code.
# Customers UserRegistry 0x64ED…073c — see GameLab ENG-0007 handoff / infra/deployments/sepolia.json.
# ENS_REGISTRAR_PK = Sepolia throwaway (fund ETH; MockUSDC is permissionless mint on 0xd332…422f).
ENS_PARENT_NAME=branchzero.eth
ENS_REGISTRAR_PK=

# ---- iNPC (OpenRouter) — product: runtime key only; lab smoke may use slots below ----
# Product design (docs/INPC.md): the *player* pastes an OpenRouter key into the iNPC Wake UI;
# it lives in sessionStorage only. It must NEVER go to the Teller Desk, Privy, localStorage,
# or a committed/product .env / VITE_* build for shipping.
# Lab ENG-0019/0020 may fill OPENROUTER_API_KEY locally for Node smoke — not a product path.
# Provider for product v1: OpenRouter only. Ollama deferred (Cloud CORS; local = install tax).
INPC_MODEL=thinkingmachines/inkling-small
# INPC_LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter   # lab/local only if a script reads it
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# LAB ONLY (never for public/hosted product builds):
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_* deferred — do not wire product to Ollama in the iNPC mission
# VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=   # forbidden on public builds
